vozero Massif, a horseshoe-shaped mountain range in the central part of the peninsula.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Lake Seydozero","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Seydozero_from_Kuyvchorr.JPG/1280px-Seydozero_from_Kuyvchorr.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Seydozero_from_Kuyvchorr.JPG/500px-Seydozero_from_Kuyvchorr.JPG","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Monfornot","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seydozero_from_Kuyvchorr.JPG"}},{"id":"murmansk_oblast_pechenga_monastery","areaId":"murmansk_oblast","name":"Pechenga Monastery","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":69.42606,"lng":31.05834},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"murmansk_oblast_pechenga_monastery","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":5,"wikiPageviews":395,"wikidataSitelinks":16,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["pechengamonastery","murmanskoblast"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"The Pechenga Monastery is and has been for many centuries the northernmost monastery in the world. It was founded in 1533 at the influx of the Pechenga River into the Barents Sea, 135 km west of modern Murmansk, by St. Tryphon, a monk from Novgorod.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Pechenga Monastery","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Pechenga_Monastery_Petsamon_luostari_01.jpg/1280px-Pechenga_Monastery_Petsamon_luostari_01.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Pechenga_Monastery_Petsamon_luostari_01.jpg/500px-Pechenga_Monastery_Petsamon_luostari_01.jpg","w":1200,"h":800,"author":"Ninaras","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pechenga_Monastery_Petsamon_luostari_01.jpg"}},{"id":"murmansk_oblast_lake_lovozero","areaId":"murmansk_oblast","name":"Lake Lovozero","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":67.85,"lng":35.16667},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"murmansk_oblast_lake_lovozero","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":1,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":234,"wikidataSitelinks":26,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["lakelovozero","murmanskoblast"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"Lake Lovozero is located on the Kola Peninsula, in Murmansk Oblast within the Barents Sea basin and ensures runoff from the river Voronya. Area: 200 km², average depth is 5.7 metres, maximal 35 m. Annual fluctuations do not exceed 1 m, and the average period of water renewal is about 10 months.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Lake Lovozero","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Lovozero_Lake.JPG/1280px-Lovozero_Lake.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Lovozero_Lake.JPG/500px-Lovozero_Lake.JPG","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Sidik iz PTU","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lovozero_Lake.JPG"}},{"id":"murmansk_oblast_valley_of_glory","areaId":"murmansk_oblast","name":"Valley of Glory","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":69.31203,"lng":32.20586},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"murmansk_oblast_valley_of_glory","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":16,"wikiPageviews":246,"wikidataSitelinks":7,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["valleyofglory","murmanskoblast"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The Valley of Glory is a valley on the right bank of the Zapadnaya Litsa River. A bloody battle began in the summer of 1941 for the region as German forces launched an offensive towards Murmansk, Russia. Russian forces halted the German assault and the frontline stabilized until the autumn of 1944.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Valley of Glory","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Russia_1._Memorial_for_the_defenders_of_the_Soviet_Arctic%2C_near_Murmansk.jpg/1280px-Russia_1._Memorial_for_the_defenders_of_the_Soviet_Arctic%2C_near_Murmansk.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Russia_1._Memorial_for_the_defenders_of_the_Soviet_Arctic%2C_near_Murmansk.jpg/500px-Russia_1._Memorial_for_the_defenders_of_the_Soviet_Arctic%2C_near_Murmansk.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Vincent van Zeijst","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Russia_1._Memorial_for_the_defenders_of_the_Soviet_Arctic,_near_Murmansk.jpg"}},{"id":"murmansk_oblast_pasvik_nature_reserve","areaId":"murmansk_oblast","name":"Pasvik Nature Reserve","category":"park","tags":["nature","hiking"],"location":{"lat":69.142,"lng":29.233},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"murmansk_oblast_pasvik_nature_reserve","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"https://pasvik-reserve.ru","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":3,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":172,"wikidataSitelinks":13,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["pasviknaturereserve","murmanskoblast"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"Pasvik Nature Reserve is a bilateral nature reserve located along the Norway–Russia border. It is located in the Pasvikdalen valley in Sør-Varanger Municipality in Finnmark county, Norway and in the Pechengsky District in Murmansk Oblast, Russia.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Pasvik Nature Reserve","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Pasvik_Zapovednik%2C_River_Paz.jpg/1280px-Pasvik_Zapovednik%2C_River_Paz.jpg","thumb":"htt